ey also have a weak hand or are pot-controlling a low pair. While a bluff might work, the pot is likely very small (limped pot), so risking chips to steal it is not mathematically attractive compared to the risk of being called by a low pair. Checking allows me to see the showdown for free and potentially win if the opponent holds a worse hand (like 8-high or lower broken draws), while preserving my chip stack.\n\nReason: I hold a very weak hand with no pair and no draw. The opponent has shown weakness by checking all streets, but my hand (9-high effectively relative to the board) unlikely beats even their bluffs or high cards. Checking back is the zero-variance play to minimize losses in a small pot while protecting my chip lead.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
